{"title":"Market Researcher Roadmap","role":"Market Researcher","summary":"A Market Researcher studies customers, markets, competitors and industry trends to help organisations make better decisions about products, pricing, positioning, expansion and marketing. The role combines business knowledge, consumer behaviour, research methodology, statistics, data analysis and communication.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 UG · 2026","Current degree":"BBA – Marketing"},"about":[{"label":"Typical degree duration","text":"3 or 4 years depending on university structure"},{"label":"Career alignment","text":"Strong/direct"},{"label":"Primary route","text":"BBA Marketing → Market Research Internship → Research Executive/Research Analyst → Market Researcher → Senior Research Analyst → Consumer Insights/Market Research Manager"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Market Research Intern, Research Executive, Research Analyst Trainee"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Consumer Insights, Market Intelligence, Brand Research, Customer Analytics or Research Consulting"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Research Analyst, Consumer Insights Specialist, Research Manager"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Consumer Insights Lead, Research Director, Strategy/Insights Leader"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a BBA – Marketing graduate, this is a strong and direct career pathway."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest future profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Marketing","Research Methodology","Statistics","Data Analytics","Consumer Psychology","AI"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Strong/direct alignment."},{"type":"p","text":"BBA Marketing provides a good foundation in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Marketing"},{"text":"Consumer behaviour"},{"text":"Business"},{"text":"Market segmentation"},{"text":"Branding"},{"text":"Sales"},{"text":"Management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should add stronger capabilities in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"SPSS/R/Python"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Consumer interviews"},{"text":"Competitive intelligence"},{"text":"Report writing"},{"text":"Presentation"}]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"These are practical planning horizons, not guaranteed promotion timelines."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Marketing + consumer behaviour"},{"text":"University + NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Consumer behaviour case study"},{"text":"Marketing foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Research methodology + Excel"},{"text":"NPTEL + Microsoft Excel","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/excel"},{"text":"Survey + Excel analysis"},{"text":"Research foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Statistics + quantitative research"},{"text":"NPTEL + statistics resources"},{"text":"Statistical research report"},{"text":"Analytical ability"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Qualitative research + Power BI"},{"text":"Industry projects + Microsoft Power BI","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/power-platform/products/power-bi"},{"text":"Consumer insights dashboard"},{"text":"Research capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Market research internship"},{"text":"Research/consulting firms"},{"text":"Internship + research report"},{"text":"Employability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Advanced analytics + specialisation"},{"text":"SQL/Python/analytics resources"},{"text":"End-to-end research project"},{"text":"Differentiation"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1 (if applicable)"},{"text":"AI + predictive research"},{"text":"AI/data analytics resources"},{"text":"Predictive consumer project"},{"text":"Future readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2 (if applicable)"},{"text":"Recruitment + portfolio"},{"text":"Employers + mock interviews"},{"text":"Job offer"},{"text":"Career entry"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core skill stack"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Market research fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Market sizing"},{"text":"Market segmentation"},{"text":"Customer profiling"},{"text":"Competitor analysis"},{"text":"Industry analysis"},{"text":"Consumer behaviour"},{"text":"Product research"},{"text":"Brand research"},{"text":"Pricing research"},{"text":"Customer satisfaction research"},{"text":"Demand estimation"},{"text":"Trend analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the research cycle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Business Question","Research Question","Methodology","Data Collection","Analysis","Insight","Recommendation"]}]},{"heading":"Research methodology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research objectives"},{"text":"Hypothesis development"},{"text":"Research questions"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Sample size concepts"},{"text":"Primary research"},{"text":"Secondary research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Exploratory research"},{"text":"Descriptive research"},{"text":"Causal research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand when each method should be used."}]},{"heading":"Survey design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to create high-quality questionnaires."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Screening questions"},{"text":"Demographic questions"},{"text":"Behavioural questions"},{"text":"Attitudinal questions"},{"text":"Rating scales"},{"text":"Ranking questions"},{"text":"Multiple-choice questions"},{"text":"Open-ended questions"},{"text":"Avoiding leading questions"},{"text":"Avoiding double-barrelled questions"},{"text":"Survey sequencing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"p","text":"Weak:"},{"type":"p","text":"“How satisfied are you with our affordable and high-quality product?”"},{"type":"p","text":"This asks about two attributes simultaneously."},{"type":"p","text":"Better:"},{"type":"p","text":"“How satisfied are you with the product's price?”"},{"type":"p","text":"and separately:"},{"type":"p","text":"“How satisfied are you with the product's quality?”"}]},{"heading":"Sampling","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Population"},{"text":"Sample"},{"text":"Sampling frame"},{"text":"Random sampling"},{"text":"Stratified sampling"},{"text":"Cluster sampling"},{"text":"Convenience sampling"},{"text":"Quota sampling"},{"text":"Sampling bias"},{"text":"Non-response bias"},{"text":"Representativeness"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should understand that a large sample does not automatically mean a representative sample."}]},{"heading":"Qualitative research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Customer interviews"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"User interviews"},{"text":"Thematic analysis"},{"text":"Coding"},{"text":"Affinity mapping"},{"text":"Customer journey research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Skills required:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Asking neutral questions"},{"text":"Active listening"},{"text":"Follow-up questioning"},{"text":"Identifying recurring themes"},{"text":"Separating evidence from interpretation"}]}]},{"heading":"Quantitative research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Median"},{"text":"Mode"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Variance"},{"text":"Percentages"},{"text":"Cross-tabulation"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Regression basics"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Statistical significance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not treat correlation as proof of causation."}]},{"heading":"Data analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Essential"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Statistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong advantage"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"R"},{"text":"SPSS"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to move from:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Raw data","Clean data","Analysis","Visualisation","Insight","Recommendation"]}]},{"heading":"Competitive intelligence","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Competitor mapping"},{"text":"Pricing comparison"},{"text":"Product comparison"},{"text":"Market positioning"},{"text":"Distribution analysis"},{"text":"Customer reviews"},{"text":"Industry trends"},{"text":"Competitor strengths/weaknesses"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Competitor","Product","Price","Positioning","Target customer","Differentiator"]}]},{"heading":"Market sizing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"TAM"},{"type":"p","text":"Total Addressable Market"},{"type":"h","text":"SAM"},{"type":"p","text":"Serviceable Available Market"},{"type":"h","text":"SOM"},{"type":"p","text":"Serviceable Obtainable Market"},{"type":"p","text":"Use transparent assumptions."},{"type":"p","text":"A good market researcher should be able to explain:"},{"type":"p","text":"Where did this number come from?"},{"type":"p","text":"rather than simply presenting a large market-size figure."}]},{"heading":"Report writing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A market researcher must convert data into a business decision."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to structure reports:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Executive Summary"},{"text":"Business Objective"},{"text":"Research Methodology"},{"text":"Sample Profile"},{"text":"Key Findings"},{"text":"Consumer Insights"},{"text":"Competitive Analysis"},{"text":"Implications"},{"text":"Recommendations"},{"text":"Limitations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The key difference is:"},{"type":"h","text":"Data ≠ Insight"},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"p","text":"“65% of respondents prefer Product A.”"},{"type":"p","text":"is a finding."},{"type":"p","text":"“Product A's preference is strongest among first-time buyers, suggesting that its simpler onboarding may be a key acquisition advantage.”"},{"type":"p","text":"is an insight/hypothesis that requires appropriate evidence."}]},{"heading":"AI for market research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn responsible use of AI for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Survey-question drafting"},{"text":"Interview transcription"},{"text":"Text classification"},{"text":"Sentiment analysis"},{"text":"Theme identification"},{"text":"Competitor research"},{"text":"Market trend analysis"},{"text":"Customer segmentation"},{"text":"Research summarisation"},{"text":"Predictive modelling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important:"},{"type":"p","text":"AI-generated market information should be validated against primary and reliable secondary sources."},{"type":"p","text":"Do not present AI-generated facts as research evidence."},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Build at least 6 strong research projects."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Consumer Behaviour Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a product category."},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research objective"},{"text":"Questionnaire"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Data collection"},{"text":"Analysis"},{"text":"Findings"},{"text":"Recommendations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Brand Perception Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Measure:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Awareness"},{"text":"Consideration"},{"text":"Preference"},{"text":"Brand associations"},{"text":"Customer satisfaction"},{"text":"Purchase intent"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Produce a professional research report."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Competitor Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Compare 5 competitors based on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pricing"},{"text":"Features"},{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Customer segment"},{"text":"Distribution"},{"text":"Reviews"},{"text":"Marketing strategy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create a competitive positioning map."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Pricing Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Price sensitivity"},{"text":"Willingness to pay"},{"text":"Competitor pricing"},{"text":"Customer segments"},{"text":"Purchase intent"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use appropriate research methods rather than treating a simple survey response as a guaranteed purchase decision."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Customer Segmentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Using appropriately sourced/synthetic data, segment customers based on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Demographics"},{"text":"Behaviour"},{"text":"Purchase frequency"},{"text":"Spending"},{"text":"Preferences"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Segment","Characteristics","Need","Opportunity","Marketing recommendation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 6 — Market Intelligence Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a Power BI dashboard covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Market size assumptions"},{"text":"Competitor data"},{"text":"Customer segments"},{"text":"Product preferences"},{"text":"Pricing"},{"text":"Trends"},{"text":"Survey findings"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation options"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Learn","Senior role"],"rows":[[{"text":"Consumer Insights"},{"text":"Research + psychology"},{"text":"Consumer behaviou